 "final_message": "All twelve items are done, and the 6 tests pass: the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones for items 9 and 10. I didn't add tests for the other fixes.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** the two new tests are in `tests/test_metrics.py`. One covers `None` counting as not converted. The other covers `dedupe_sessions` keeping the last session when ids repeat.\n- **Item 11:** the README entry for `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries. I also added the `daily_conversion_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** the rest of the package also broke the spec, so I fixed three more functions:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts the keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` now resets the streak when a day has no flagged sessions.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise `ValueError` with the line number in that case. Say so if you'd rather it did something else.",
